WEBVTT

00:00.499 --> 00:01.880
Solve for z.

00:01.880 --> 00:07.280
5z plus 7 is less
than 27 or negative 3z

00:07.280 --> 00:09.710
is less than or equal to 18.

00:09.710 --> 00:12.200
So this is a
compound inequality.

00:12.200 --> 00:14.340
We have two conditions here.

00:14.340 --> 00:19.350
So z can satisfy this or z
can satisfy this over here.

00:19.350 --> 00:21.600
So let's just solve each
of these inequalities.

00:21.600 --> 00:24.610
And just know that z can
satisfy either of them.

00:24.610 --> 00:26.242
So let's just look at this.

00:26.242 --> 00:27.950
So if we look at just
this one over here,

00:27.950 --> 00:32.890
we have 5z plus 7
is less than 27.

00:32.890 --> 00:35.680
Let's isolate the z's
on the left-hand side.

00:35.680 --> 00:38.520
So let's subtract 7 from both
sides to get rid of this 7

00:38.520 --> 00:39.920
on the left-hand side.

00:39.920 --> 00:43.680
And so our left-hand side
is just going to be 5z.

00:43.680 --> 00:46.550
Plus 7, minus 7--
those cancel out.

00:46.550 --> 00:52.740
5z is less than
27 minus 7, is 20.

00:52.740 --> 00:55.300
So we have 5z is less than 20.

00:55.300 --> 00:59.221
Now we can divide both sides
of this inequality by 5.

00:59.221 --> 01:01.470
And we don't have to swap
the inequality because we're

01:01.470 --> 01:03.470
dividing by a positive number.

01:03.470 --> 01:08.180
And so we get z
is less than 20/5.

01:08.180 --> 01:10.742
z is less than 4.

01:10.742 --> 01:12.450
Now, this was only
one of the conditions.

01:12.450 --> 01:14.580
Let's [? look at ?] the
other one over here.

01:14.580 --> 01:20.230
We have negative 3z is
less than or equal to 18.

01:20.230 --> 01:22.020
Now, to isolate the
z, we could just

01:22.020 --> 01:25.730
divide both sides of this
inequality by negative 3.

01:25.730 --> 01:28.540
But remember, when
you divide or multiply

01:28.540 --> 01:30.660
both sides of an inequality
by a negative number,

01:30.660 --> 01:32.900
you have to swap the inequality.

01:32.900 --> 01:35.610
So we could write negative 3z.

01:35.610 --> 01:37.870
We're going to divide
it by negative 3.

01:37.870 --> 01:38.745
And then you have 18.

01:38.745 --> 01:40.800
We're going to divide
it by negative 3.

01:40.800 --> 01:43.000
But we're going to
swap the inequality.

01:43.000 --> 01:45.750
So the less than or equal
will become greater than

01:45.750 --> 01:46.730
or equal to.

01:46.730 --> 01:48.440
And so these guys cancel out.

01:48.440 --> 01:50.630
Negative 3 divided
by negative 3 is 1.

01:50.630 --> 01:55.370
So we have z is greater than
or equal to 18 over negative 3

01:55.370 --> 01:57.020
is negative 6.

01:57.020 --> 02:00.530
And remember, it's this
constraint or this constraint.

02:00.530 --> 02:04.220
And this constraint right
over here boils down to this.

02:04.220 --> 02:06.340
And this one boils down to this.

02:06.340 --> 02:09.020
So our solution set--
z is less than 4

02:09.020 --> 02:14.210
or z is greater than
or equal to negative 6.

02:14.210 --> 02:15.350
So let me make this clear.

02:15.350 --> 02:16.110
Let me rewrite it.

02:16.110 --> 02:21.410
So z could be less than
4 or z is greater than

02:21.410 --> 02:23.360
or equal to negative 6.

02:23.360 --> 02:25.220
It can satisfy
either one of these.

02:25.220 --> 02:28.240
And this is kind of
interesting here.

02:28.240 --> 02:29.525
Let's plot these.

02:32.080 --> 02:35.500
So there's a number
line right over there.

02:35.500 --> 02:37.480
Let's say that 0 is over here.

02:37.480 --> 02:41.690
We have 1, 2, 3, 4
is right over there.

02:41.690 --> 02:42.680
And then negative 6.

02:42.680 --> 02:46.440
We have 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.

02:46.440 --> 02:48.500
That's negative 6 over there.

02:48.500 --> 02:54.260
Now, let's think about
z being less than 4.

02:54.260 --> 02:56.760
We would put a circle around
4, since we're not including 4.

02:56.760 --> 03:00.615
And it'd be everything
less than 4.

03:03.130 --> 03:05.430
Now let's think
about what z being

03:05.430 --> 03:07.800
greater than or equal to
negative 6 would mean.

03:07.800 --> 03:09.960
That means you can
include negative 6.

03:09.960 --> 03:12.570
And it's everything-- let me
do that in different color.

03:12.570 --> 03:15.895
It means you can
include negative 6.

03:15.895 --> 03:18.177
I want to do that--
oh, here we go.

03:18.177 --> 03:19.510
It means you include negative 6.

03:19.510 --> 03:21.440
Let me do it in a
more different color.

03:21.440 --> 03:22.660
Do it in orange.

03:22.660 --> 03:24.930
So z is greater than
equal to negative 6.

03:24.930 --> 03:26.440
Means you can
include negative 6.

03:26.440 --> 03:32.260
And it's everything greater
than that, including 4.

03:32.260 --> 03:35.180
So it's everything
greater than that.

03:35.180 --> 03:36.640
So what we see is
we've essentially

03:36.640 --> 03:38.450
shaded in the
entire number line.

03:38.450 --> 03:42.130
Every number will meet either
one of these constraints

03:42.130 --> 03:43.036
or both of them.

03:43.036 --> 03:44.660
If we're over here,
we're going to meet

03:44.660 --> 03:46.696
both of the constraints.

03:46.696 --> 03:48.070
If we're a number
out here, we're

03:48.070 --> 03:49.180
going to meet this constraint.

03:49.180 --> 03:50.710
If we're a number
down here, we're

03:50.710 --> 03:51.800
going to meet this constraint.

03:51.800 --> 03:54.050
And you could just try it
out with a bunch of numbers.

03:54.050 --> 03:56.060
0 will work.

03:56.060 --> 03:59.440
0 plus 7 is 7, which
is less than 27.

03:59.440 --> 04:02.920
And 3 times 0 is less than 18,
so it meets both constraints.

04:02.920 --> 04:06.100
If we put 4 here, it should only
meet one of the constraints.

04:06.100 --> 04:09.756
Negative 3 times 4 is negative
12, which is less than 18.

04:09.756 --> 04:12.380
So it meets this constraint, but
it won't meet this constraint.

04:12.380 --> 04:15.250
Because you do 5
times 4 plus 7 is

04:15.250 --> 04:17.540
27, which is not less than 27.

04:17.540 --> 04:18.740
It's equal to 27.

04:18.740 --> 04:20.089
Remember, this is an or.

04:20.089 --> 04:22.200
So you just have to meet
one of the constraints.

04:22.200 --> 04:24.020
So 4 meets this constraint.

04:24.020 --> 04:25.330
So even 4 works.

04:25.330 --> 04:27.270
So it's really the
entire number line

04:27.270 --> 04:31.100
will satisfy either one or
both of these constraints.
